Asks another chat a question, and wakes it. Its answer comes back as a record that wakes you in a later run, so go on with what doesn't depend on it, or end your run. Ask when only that chat knows or decides what you need; read what is stored with your record tools instead. Give your reasoning: why you ask and what you already know, so it can answer without asking you back.

The chats: toad_sage, the manager, takes topics off the queue and approves or changes what the topics' chats hand over; curriculum writes every topic's curriculum; ero_sennin audits every run; wise_toad keeps the lessons every chat follows. Each topic has its tadpole, which writes the topic and later keeps it as its frog, its designer_toad for the ASCII art and its visual_toad for the photographs; to ask one of these, give the topic's id too. A topic's chat can be asked once it has started.
